{
  "component": "Date Input Field",
  "description": "A three-part date entry field with separate day, month and year boxes, wrapped by an optional label, description and error message. Ten variants cover five states (Default, Error, Disabled, Hover, Focus) against two value types (Default and Placeholder).\n\nPURPOSE: Captures a date as three short numeric segments rather than one free-text string. Each segment is its own input frame, so DD, MM and YYYY can be validated and focused independently. The label, description and error text are text properties, so the same component serves birth dates, expiry dates, start dates and so on.\n\nBEHAVIOUR: The State property carries the visual response to interaction. Hover and Focus change the border treatment, Focus uses Border/Focus/Default. Error swaps the border to Border/Danger/Default and reveals the Error text layer, which only exists in the two Error components. Disabled applies Background/Disabled/Default, Border/Disabled/default and Text/Disabled/Default across the group. Value Type switches between a filled value and placeholder text, with placeholder content sitting on Text/Default/Tertiary.\n\nCOMPOSITION: No nested component instances were detected. The three Input frames inside the Inputs row are plain frames, each holding a single text layer. Label, Description and Error are direct text layers on the component. If the development codebase already has a text input or field wrapper, AI code generators should reuse it for the three segments and for the label and error slots rather than writing new markup.\n\nUSAGE: Use this when a date must be typed and the parts matter separately, for example validating a month before a day. Use a single text input with a date mask if the date is pasted or copied often. Use a calendar or picker when the user is choosing from a range or needs to see surrounding days. Keep Has Description off unless the format or constraint needs explaining, and reserve the Error state for a resolved validation failure.\n\nCODE GENERATION NOTES: Group the three segments in one fieldset with the label as its legend or an aria-labelledby reference, so screen readers announce one date field, not three unlabelled boxes. Auto-advance focus from DD to MM to YYYY once a segment is complete, and allow Backspace to step back. Accept pasted full dates into the first segment and split them. The Error state in Figma shows border colour plus a text message, so keep both and wire the message with aria-describedby and aria-invalid. Disabled must set the disabled attribute on all three inputs, not just the styling. Hover and Focus are CSS states and should not become props.",
